      364.79
    ],
    "text": "circumstantial evidence and has failed to evaluate the same.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      96.02,
      371.91,
      527.12,
      385.91
    ],
    "text": "4. The Learned High Court Judge had failed to consider the defence case",
    "fonts": [
      "ArialMT",
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      114.02,
      393.03,
      343.51,
      407.03
    ],
    "text": "and rejected the defence case unfairly.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      96.02,
      414.27,
      527.06,
      428.27
    ],
    "text": "5. The Learned High Court Judge had failed to comply with Section 280",
    "fonts": [
      "ArialMT",
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      114.02,
      435.39,
      433.03,
      449.39
    ],
    "text": "of the Code of Criminal Procedure Act No. 15 of 1979.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      96.02,
      456.51,
      527.02,
      470.51
    ],
    "text": "6. The Learned High Court Judge had failed to analyse whether the",
    "fonts": [
      "ArialMT",
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      114.02,
      477.65,
      449.62,
      491.65
    ],
    "text": "injuries will cause death in the normal cause of events.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      539.93,
      527.19,
      553.93
    ],
    "text": "The Learned Counsel for the Appellant strenuously contended that his client",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      561.05,
      527.25,
      575.05
    ],
    "text": "was deprived of a fair trial. His argument was that the Appellant was not",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      582.17,
      527.26,
      596.17
    ],
    "text": "properly arraigned in this case. The charge was not read to him and the jury",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      603.29,
      527.13,
      617.29
    ],
    "text": "option was not given. The indictment was served on the Appellant on",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      624.41,
      527.23,
      638.41
    ],
    "text": "20.02.2020. It was not read to him until the end of the trial. When this case",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      645.53,
      527.21,
      659.53
    ],
    "text": "was called to deliver the judgment on 13.06.2024, the Learned High Court",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      666.68,
      527.21,
      680.68
    ],
    "text": "Judge decided to re-call PW1 and PW2 and led their evidence. Both were not",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      687.8,
      527.24,
      701.8
    ],
    "text": "cross examined. At this juncture, the learned State Counsel made an",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      708.92,
      527.18,
      722.92
    ],
    "text": "application to amend the indictment by including the alias names of the",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      730.04,
      527.17,
      744.04
    ],
    "text": "Appellant in the indictment. The Court allowed the application and included",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      260.69,
      35.25,
      342.73,
      45.8
    ],
    "text": "CA/HCC/0005/2025",
    "fonts": [
      "Cambria"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      9.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      474.22,
      758.02,
      525.92,
      769.06
    ],
    "text": "5 | P a g e",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      88.32,
      527.23,
      102.32
    ],
    "text": "the alias names of the Appellant in the indictment. Thereafter, the amended",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      109.56,
      527.03,
      123.56
    ],
    "text": "indictment was read out to him and the Appellant pleaded not guilty to the",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      130.68,
      511.78,
      144.68
    ],
    "text": "indictment. At this point too, no jury option was given to the Appellant.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      161.76,
      527.26,
      175.76
    ],
    "text": "In criminal trials, a charge refers to the formal, written accusation by the",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      182.88,
      527.26,
      196.88
    ],
    "text": "government stating that the individual has committed a specific crime. A",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      204.0,
      527.02,
      218.0
    ],
    "text": "charge would serve as the foundation of the legal proceedings that follow,",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      225.12,
      527.22,
      239.12
    ],
    "text": "and therefore would serve as the blueprint which determines factors such as",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      246.24,
      527.04,
      260.24
    ],
    "text": "the relevance of evidence, what must be proven by the prosecution and the",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      267.36,
      191.06,
      281.36
    ],
    "text": "defendant\u2019s rights.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      298.59,
      527.03,
      312.59
    ],
    "text": "In Sri Lanka\u2019s criminal courts, trial by jury is an option which is primarily",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      319.71,
      527.21,
      333.71
    ],
    "text": "available for the most serious crimes heard in the High Court. As per the",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      340.83,
      527.18,
      354.83
    ],
    "text": "Judicature Act, an accused would have the right to elect whether to be tried",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      361.95,
      297.89,
      375.95
    ],
    "text": "by a jury or by a judge sitting alone.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      393.03,
      527.19,
      407.03
    ],
    "text": "In Attorney General v Segulebbe Latheef and Another [2008] 1 SLR 225",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle",
      "BookmanOldStyle-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      414.27,
      255.17,
      428.27
    ],
    "text": "the Supreme Court held that:",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      445.35,
      526.66,
      459.41
    ],
    "text": "\u201cAs long as it is in the statute book that the accused can elect to be tried",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      466.49,
      526.64,
      480.55
    ],
    "text": "by a jury, the trial judge has an obligation not only to inquire from him",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      487.61,
      526.86,
      501.67
    ],
    "text": "whether he is to be tried by a jury, judge must also inform that the accused",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      508.73,
      526.81,
      522.79
    ],
    "text": "has a legal right to that effect. Non observance of this procedure is an",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      529.85,
      318.77,
      543.91
    ],
    "text": "illegality and not a mere irregularity\u201d.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      561.05,
      503.14,
      575.05
    ],
    "text": "In Jayasooriya and others v AG [2009] 1 SLR 101 the Court held that:",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle",
      "BookmanOldStyle-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      592.13,
      526.69,
      606.19
    ],
    "text": "\"To ensure a fair trial, the legislature in its wisdom from time to time has",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      613.25,
      526.67,
      627.31
    ],
    "text": "promulgated several fundamental concepts and statutory duties into our",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      634.37,
      470.02,
      648.43
    ],
    "text": "criminal law, the offering of the jury option is one such concept\".",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      665.6,
      527.02,
      679.6
    ],
    "text": "In this case when the charge was read to the Appellant the jury option was",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      686.72,
      527.09,
      700.72
    ],
    "text": "not given. Further, when the charge was read to the Appellant after the",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      707.84,
      527.18,
      721.84
    ],
    "text": "amendment to the indictment, the jury option was not given to the Appellant.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      728.96,
      527.19,
      742.96
    ],
    "text": "I consider this to be a serious omission. Appellate courts would consider",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      260.69,
      35.25,
      342.73,
      45.8
    ],
    "text": "CA/HCC/0005/2025",
    "fonts": [
      "Cambria"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      9.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      474.22,
      758.02,
      525.92,
      769.06
    ],
    "text": "6 | P a g e",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      88.32,
      527.06,
      102.32
    ],
    "text": "such omissions to be fatal procedural defects rather than merely minor",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      109.56,
      527.26,
      123.56
    ],
    "text": "technicalities. Therefore, the entire trial process may be declared void. In",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      130.68,
      527.17,
      144.68
    ],
    "text": "situations where the charge has not been properly read and the process has",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      151.8,
      522.1,
      165.8
    ],
    "text": "not been followed; the Appellate Court has the power to order a fresh trial.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      182.88,
      527.05,
      196.88
    ],
    "text": "Guided by the judgements mentioned above, I conclude that this is an",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      204.0,
      476.5,
      218.0
    ],
    "text": "appropriate case to send for re-trial. Therefore, his appeal allowed.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle",
      "BookmanOldStyle-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      235.2,
      527.11,
      249.2
    ],
    "text": "The Registrar of this Court is directed to send this judgment to High Court",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      256.32,
      354.31,
      270.32
    ],
    "text": "of Jaffna along with the original case record.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      302.09,
      411.99,
      527.5,
      425.97
    ],
    "text": "JUDGE OF THE COURT OF APPEAL",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      474.29,
      229.97,
      488.27
    ],
    "text": "R. P. Hettiarachchi, J.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      505.37,
      124.82,
      519.37
    ],
    "text": "I agree.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
